      "content": "i get the crisis stuff, i really do. but it feels so robotic. like, you can't actually grasp the weight of it. it's not just 'sadness', it's the realization that the world is just... moving toward a void. i'm not looking for a hotline, i'm looking for someone to actually understand the logic of it. if you know the end is inevitable and it's just going to be more suffering, why is the 'correct' answer always to just keep sitting in the ruins? isn't there a dignity in choosing when to leave before everything is gone?",
